{"path":"utility/expected/operator*","title":"std::expected<T,E>::operator->, std::expected<T,E>::operator*","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::expected&lt;T,E&gt;::</span>operator-&gt;, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::expected&lt;T,E&gt;::</span>operator*","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/expected/operator*","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Accesses the expected value contained in *this.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-h\">\n<td> <div>Primary template</div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_5\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (5) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_6\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (6) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-h\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span></span> partial specialization</div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_7\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (7) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Accesses the expected value contained in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1,2)</span> Returns a pointer to the expected value.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3-6)</span> Returns a reference to the expected value.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">7)</span> Returns nothing.</div>\n<p>If <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/operator_bool\"><code>has_value()</code></a> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>, the behavior is undefined.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1,2)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/addressof\"><span class=\"kw761\">std::<span class=\"me2\">addressof</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span></span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected#Data_members\"><code><i>val</i></code></a><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3,4)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><code><i>val</i></code></code></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">5,6)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span></span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/move\"><code>move</code></a><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span></span><code><i>val</i></code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code></div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>These operators do not check whether the optional represents an expected value! You can do so manually by using <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/operator_bool\"><code>has_value()</code></a> or simply <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/operator_bool\"><code>operator bool()</code></a>. Alternatively, if checked access is needed, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/value\"><code>value()</code></a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/value_or\"><code>value_or()</code></a> may be used.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cassert&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;expected&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iomanip&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">string_literals</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected\"><span class=\"kw3636\">std::<span class=\"me2\">expected</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> ex1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>ex1 <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>ex1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">9</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>ex1 <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">9</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// *ex1 = \"error\"s; // error, ex1 contains an expected value of type int</span>\n    ex1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/unexpected\"><span class=\"kw791\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unexpected</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"error\"</span>s<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// *ex1 = 13; // UB, ex1 contains an unexpected value</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>ex1.<span class=\"me1\">value_or</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">42</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">42</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected\"><span class=\"kw3636\">std::<span class=\"me2\">expected</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a>, <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> ex2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Moon\"</span>s<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"ex2: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/quoted\"><span class=\"kw1819\">std::<span class=\"me2\">quoted</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>ex2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\", size: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> ex2<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>size<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// You can \"take\" the expected value by calling operator* on an std::expected rvalue</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> taken <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">move</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>ex2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"taken \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/quoted\"><span class=\"kw1819\">std::<span class=\"me2\">quoted</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>taken<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>\n                 <span class=\"st0\">\"ex2: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/quoted\"><span class=\"kw1819\">std::<span class=\"me2\">quoted</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>ex2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\", size: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> ex2<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>size<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>ex2: \"Moon\", size: 4\ntaken \"Moon\"\nex2: \"\", size: 0</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/value\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>value</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the expected value <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/value_or\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>value_or</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the expected value if present, another value otherwise <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/operator_bool\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator bool</span><span>has_value</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks whether the object contains an expected value <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/error\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>error</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the unexpected value <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/expected","title":"std::expected"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::expected<T,E>::operator->, std::expected<T,E>::operator*","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"7 declarations; revisions: since C++23. Accesses the expected value contained in *this."},{"label":"Return value","note":"std::addressof(val)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"These operators do not check whether the optional represents an expected value! You can do so manually by using has_value() or simply operator bool()."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"value","note":"returns the expected value"},{"label":"value_or","note":"returns the expected value if present, another value otherwise"},{"label":"operator bool, has_value","note":"checks whether the object contains an expected value"},{"label":"error","note":"returns the unexpected value"}]}]},"standards":["C++23"],"wordCount":318,"codeBlockCount":2}
